<<
/A 2107 0 R
/Alt (Two side-by-side scatter plots labeled \(a\) and \(b\) show cost saving percentage versus escape risk epsilon. Both plots feature light blue points for candidate subsets, a black curve for the approximate Pareto front, and a dashed red vertical line indicating a quality threshold with a red star at its intersection. Plot \(a\) displays a wider, upward trend in cost savings with increasing risk, fitting a logarithmic trend, while plot \(b\) shows higher clustered cost savings and minimal escape risk. Legends identify all visual indicators.)
